# Rent Manager

Vite/React/Redux UI in `app/` (`app/` alias of `app/src/`). Express ticker in `server/`. Pago SDK in `server/lib/`. Env files stay at the repo root. Redux via `app/core/store`.

## Style

- No semicolons, no trailing commas, double quotes, 2-space indent, max 160 cols
- Prefer lodash (`import _ from "lodash"`) at call site over one-off helpers or native equivalents
- No one-off named helpers/wrappers — extract only when reused 2+ times
- Destructure with `|| {}` / `|| []`; avoid `?.` for field reads (optional calls OK)
- No nested ternaries; name booleans. JSX: `&&` not ternary. Imperative: `if`, not `&&`
- No defensive code: no try/catch unless recovering; no fallbacks for required data/env
- Little noise: persist actual payloads; no remaps; `cleanDeep` means no null guards
- Rem for custom sizes (often `0.75rem`). Minimal diffs
- Store collections: `{ [id]: { id, ... } }`. Constants stay arrays. Iterate with `Object.values` / `Object.keys` / lodash
- React UI state via `actions` so handlers live in `actions.js`
- Scope store paths with `actions.create(path | () => path)`

## UI (`app/`)

- Imports from `app/` (alias of `src/`): `core/`, `screens/`, `components/`
- `actions`/`store` from `app/core/store`
- `React.useState` etc. — never destructure built-ins from `"react"` (third-party hooks unprefixed)
- Redux only: `actions.get/set/update/unset`; `useSelector(() => selectX())`; fetch then select
- Selectors return the store slice (`EMPTY_OBJECT` / `EMPTY_ARRAY`) or find by id. No `Object.values` / filter / map in selectors — iterate in the component
- Domain modules: selectors → fetchers → mutators. Fetchers write store only
- Loaders: `setLoader`/`clearLoader`. No nested components
- Mantine + Tailwind + `cn()` from `app/core`. Persist via `PERSISTENT_PATHS`
- Every UI element has a stable kebab-case class as the first `cn()` argument
- Plain dark chrome: `#111`, system UI, no display type or brand accent
- Quiet section labels, bordered cards, in-page / header actions
- Mantine components over custom chrome. `NumberInput` for numeric values
